{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0796-decentralized-aggregation-llm-wagering.md", "equation": "The weighted-score wagering mechanism (Lambert et al.): payout $\\pi_i = w_i (s(p_i,y) - \\bar s_w)$, where $\\bar s_w$ is the wager-weighted average score. Problem: the optimal wager is **binary** (0 or max) — too coarse for weighting — and incentive compatibility relies on immutable beliefs.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9129}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0796-decentralized-aggregation-llm-wagering.md", "equation": "2. **Theorem 3.3 (Advantage–wager alignment).** For any fixed prediction, the best-response wager is $w_i^*(p_i) = (A_i / 2c_3)^+$, where $A_i = \\mathbb{E}[s(p_i,Y) - b_{-i} \\mid \\mathcal{F}_i]$ is the expected score advantage. Agents with non-positive advantage wager **zero** and self-exclude from aggregation. This is a continuous, informative weight signal — not binary.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9129}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0796-decentralized-aggregation-llm-wagering.md", "equation": "WALLA I:** $b_{-i} = \\sum_{j \\ne i} w_j s(p_j,y) / \\sum_{j \\ne i} w_j$ (average of scores). Satisfies normality; admits arbitrage.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9129}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0796-decentralized-aggregation-llm-wagering.md", "equation": "WALLA II:** $b_{-i} = s(q_{-i}, y)$ with $q_{-i} = \\sum_{j \\ne i} w_j p_j / \\sum_{j \\ne i} w_j$ (score of the pooled prediction). Satisfies no-arbitrage; sacrifices normality.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9129}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0796-decentralized-aggregation-llm-wagering.md", "equation": "Linear pooling $\\hat p_{\\text{lin}} = \\sum_i w_i p_i / W$ (minimizer of wager-weighted KL$(p_i \\| q)$, preserves disagreement) and logarithmic pooling $\\hat p_{\\log}[y] \\propto \\prod_i p_i[y]^{w_i/W}$ (externally Bayesian, sharper, consensus-emphasizing). Experiments show the learned wagers, not the pooling choice, drive quality.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9129}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0796-decentralized-aggregation-llm-wagering.md", "equation": "Each agent freezes its base LLM and trains a small 2-layer MLP on its last-layer hidden state to output a non-negative wager. Training signal: the **hindsight-optimal wager** $w^* = ((s_i - b_{-i})/2c_3)^+$, recovered from the agent's **own** payout alone via $s_i - b_{-i} = \\pi_i / w_i + c_3 w_i$ — fully decentralized. MSE objective to the hindsight target is equivalent to hindsight regret minimization when $w^* > 0$.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9129}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0796-decentralized-aggregation-llm-wagering.md", "equation": "WALLA I (M=4): AUC 81.07 ± 0.58, ACC 87.00 ± 0.47 — matches StackedGen (81.99/87.76) and RouteLLM w/ context (82.32/87.48), beats all decentralized/learning-free baselines.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9129}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0796-decentralized-aggregation-llm-wagering.md", "equation": "Target: hindsight-optimal wager $w^* = ((s_i - b_{-i})/2c_3)^+$.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9129}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0796-decentralized-aggregation-llm-wagering.md", "equation": "1. Per completed game, compute each signal source's Brier score $s_i$ and the leave-one-out weighted baseline $b_{-i} = \\sum_{j \\ne i} w_j s_j / \\sum_{j \\ne i} w_j$ (WALLA I).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9129}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0796-decentralized-aggregation-llm-wagering.md", "equation": "2. Hindsight target $w_i^* = ((s_i - b_{-i})/2c_3)^+$ with $c_3$ tuned so mean wager ≈ 1 (deficit lever is irrelevant internally).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9129}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0796-decentralized-aggregation-llm-wagering.md", "equation": "4. Aggregate game probabilities with linear pooling $\\hat p = \\sum_i w_i p_i / W$; fall back to equal weights when $\\sum_i w_i \\approx 0$.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9129}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0796-decentralized-aggregation-llm-wagering.md", "equation": "Improvement experiment:** Replace the scalar advantage target with a **decision-weighted advantage** $A_i^{dec} = u \\cdot (s_i - b_{-i})$ where $u$ is realized CLV or Kelly fraction for the game — the paper uses statistical scores only, but ledger 0791 showed statistical-score optimization can be financially suboptimal; test whether decision-weighted wagers beat score-weighted wagers on realized profit.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9129}
