{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0812-deep-generative-models-synthetic-financial-data.md", "equation": "Log-returns r_t = ln(P_t/P_{t−1}); standardized r̃_t = (r_t − μ_r)/σ_r. Portfolio: R_t = w'r_t; μ_p = E[R_t]; σ²_p = w'Σw. Markowitz: min_w w'Σw s.t. w'1=1, w'μ=μ*_p. Lagrangian L(w,λ,γ) = w'Σw − λ(w'μ−μ_p) − γ(w'1−1); w* = Σ^{−1}(λμ/2 + γ1/2) with the 2×2 system for (λ/2, γ/2). Generative framing: synthetic r̃_{1:T} = G_θ(z), z~p(z), minimizing divergence (KL/Wasserstein) to p(r_{1:T}). GARCH(1,1), VaR, ES as above. DTW(X_real,X_syn) = min_π Σ_{(i,j)∈π} | . Sharpe = E[R_p−R_f]/σ_p; Sortino = E[R_p−R_f]/σ_d; MaxDD = (max P_t − min P_t)/max P_t.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9129}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0813-diversification-limited-information-kelly-game.md", "equation": "(1) M simultaneous identical independent games: G = Σ_{w=0}^{M} P(w;M,p)·ln[1+(2w−M)f], P binomial; optimum from Σ_w P(w;M,p)/[1+(2w−M)f] = 1 (Eq. 9). Exact closed forms for M=1,2; approximations for M≥5.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9129}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0813-diversification-limited-information-kelly-game.md", "equation": "(2) Insider–outsider: insider knows p exactly on one game whose true win prob alternates between p±Δ; outsider plays M games knowing only mean p. Threshold Δ(p,M) from G_I(p,Δ) = G_O(p,M).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9129}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0813-diversification-limited-information-kelly-game.md", "equation": "(3) Finite memory: investor sees only last L outcomes (w wins); Bayesian posterior with uniform prior π(p)=1 gives ϱ(p|w,L) = (L+1)!/[w!(L−w)!]·p^w(1−p)^{L−w}; optimal fraction f*(w,L) = (2w−L)/(L+2) for w≥L/2, else 0 (no shorting).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9129}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0813-diversification-limited-information-kelly-game.md", "equation": "Single game: f_K(p) = 2p−1; G_K(p) = ln 2 − S(p), S(p) = −[p ln p + (1−p) ln(1−p)]; R_K(p) = 2·p^p(1−p)^{1−p} − 1. Example: p=0.6 → f_K=0.2, R_K = 2.0% (vs naive 20% expected return).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9129}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0813-diversification-limited-information-kelly-game.md", "equation": "M games, unsaturated (Mf*≪1): f*(p) = (2p−1)/[M(2p−1)² + 4p(1−p)] (Eq. 10). For p−1/2 ≪ 1/M reduces to f* = 2p−1 per game (games decouple). Diverse games: f*_i = 2p_i−1.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9129}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0813-diversification-limited-information-kelly-game.md", "equation": "M games, saturated (1−Mf*≪1): f* = (1/M)[1 − 2p(1−p)^M/(2p−1)] (Eq. 11); join at p_c where the two approximations intersect.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9129}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0813-diversification-limited-information-kelly-game.md", "equation": "Insider growth: G_I = ½[ln 2 + S(p+Δ)] if p−Δ ≤ 1/2; = ½[ln 2 + S(p+Δ)] + ½[ln 2 + S(p−Δ)] if p−Δ > 1/2. Threshold: Δ(p,M) ≈ (p−1/2)(√(2M)−1) for small edge.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9129}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0813-diversification-limited-information-kelly-game.md", "equation": "Finite memory: f*(w,L) = (2w−L)/(L+2); G(p,L) ≈ G_K(p) − 1/(2L) (Eq. 19); L_min ≈ 1/[2·G_K(p)]; full series Eq. 20 to O(1/L³).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9129}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0813-diversification-limited-information-kelly-game.md", "equation": "p=0.6: f_K = 0.2, per-turn expected return at Kelly = 4%, compounded R_K = 2.0%.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9129}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0813-diversification-limited-information-kelly-game.md", "equation": "M=2 exact: f*_2 = (2p−1)/(4p²−4p+2).", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9129}
{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0813-diversification-limited-information-kelly-game.md", "equation": "Minimum memory for profitability: p=0.51 → L ≥ 1,761; p=0.52 → L ≥ 438 (both exact as stated). General rule: L_min ≈ 1/[2·G_K(p)].", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9129}
